{
  "borough": "London Borough of Barking and Dagenham",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:justify&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;The&amp;nbsp;proposed development fails to provide sufficient information with respect to transport impacts and subsequent mitigation measures. In the absence of such, the proposal is likely significantly impact the accessibility of the site and the surrounding area, and is likely to impact access and egress,&amp;nbsp; result in increased parking pressure and impact the operations of the site. The proposal fails to demonstrate safe and adequate car and cycle parking and safe access for pedestrians and cyclists entering the site.&amp;nbsp; The proposal is therefore likely to result in a detrimental impact on highway safety and the existing transport network, to the detriment of sustainable travel principles. It is therefore contrary to the following:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;The National Planning Policy Framework&amp;nbsp;(NPPF) (DLUHC, December 2023)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;Policies T3, T5 and T6 of the London Plan (March 2021)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;Policy CM1 of the&amp;nbsp;Local Development Framework Core Strategy (July 2010)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;Policies BR9, BR10 and BR11 of the&amp;nbsp;Local Development Framework Borough Wide Development Plan Document (March 2011)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;Policies SP8, DMM1, DMSI 8, DMT2 and DMT3 of&amp;nbsp;The London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Draft Local Plan: (Regulation 19 Submission Version, December 2021)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;"
  ],
